id: pm-web-cnhi
title: Expose current evidence fragments through the supported SDK
description: "pm-web inspection cannot render an unchanged unretained JSON-pointer fragment using the published pm-evidence SDK. check(diff:true) emits current text only for changed fragments; replay requires retained original bytes; show omits bytes. The existing exact resolveFragment(text, descriptor): Fragment implementation is private. A minimal validated public export or read-only check option must expose the same resolver and raw spans without writes or duplicate source resolution. Discovered while repairing pm-web-5sx6 and PR 278; sibling-repository authorization is pending."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[1]: sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-29T06:47:11.915Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T07:14:59.378Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A public pm-evidence SDK operation returns exact live raw fragments independently of original retention; producer schemas validate its inputs and outputs; escaped JSON pointers, raw number spellings, prototype-named members, root selection, changed sources and malformed retained originals are covered; npm and Bun packed consumers use the supported root export; pm-web uses the approved SDK commit and its current-fragment regression passes."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T06:48:45.763Z",codex-agent,"The published pm-evidence 2026.10.28 root declarations were checked: check returns diff.current only for changed freshness, replay requires retained original bytes, and show returns metadata. The latest public main bundle API exports only already-retained bytes under consent and does not solve live resolution. The existing private resolveFragment(text, descriptor): Fragment must become a validated supported export (or check must offer exact current fragments). Installed CLI SDK declarations and open upstream issue searches yielded no supported equivalent. The five-span regression uses real SDK state and exact source spellings; no JSON parse/stringify normalization can satisfy it for large integers and exponents. No sibling repository has been modified; the required scope decision remains pending."
  "2026-10-29T07:11:26.792Z",codex-agent,"The linked source-security suite was rerun through the owning feature item: 6 tests total, 5 passed and the live JSON test failed with five null fragments where exact raw spans were expected; no tests were weakened, deleted or skipped. A supported SDK export remains required before this item can be implemented. The original feature item now records this item as its blocker."
  "2026-10-29T07:14:59.378Z",codex-agent,"The broader regression now covers 18 cases across line, heading and JSON-pointer selectors, both current and changed sources, and absent, valid or corrupt retained originals. It fails because current text depends on historical replay in every selector family; inspection still preserves native state read back through the SDK. This is the same blocker class, not a JSON-only display special case. Both failing tests remain enabled. Repair requires the same exact pm-evidence resolver for current text and diff:false verification so bad historical replay cannot suppress live facts."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  src/services/evidence-inspection.ts,project
  test/evidence-source-security.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
